# Customer Preview Contract

Customer-facing output must **never** expose:
- Internal notes
- Labour hour workings (`Allow N hours to…`)
- Pricing facts or line item rates
- Matched JMS lines or item codes
- Account codes or tax codes
- `[]` placeholders

## Required sections (when data is present)

| Section | Source |
|---|---|
| Scope of Work | `customer_scope` + `primary_quote.scope` (filtered) |
| Materials | `quote.materials` |
| Optional Works | `optional_quotes[].scope` |
| Exclusions | `quote.exclusions` |

## Internal review must preserve (not shown to customer)

- Labour quantities (hours per task, total hours)
- Material quantities and flags
- Assumptions and missing information
- Warnings and review notices
- Account codes, tax codes, item/source mappings

## Assembler guard rules

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — internal note leaks to customer
sections: [{ title: "Notes", items: ["This is not a retaining wall"] }]

// ✅ GOOD — internal notes filtered before assembly
isInternalNote(value) → strip from all customer-facing sections
isLabourLine(value)   → strip from all customer-facing sections
```
